  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of Two 17th-Century Temples in Bulgan Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 17th-century temples in the Khugnu Khan Natural Protected Area are important for their unique architectural style and connection to historical events, representing Mongolian, Tibetan, and Chinese influences. The project aims to restore and preserve the original structure and design of these temples, ensuring their longevity and cultural heritage for future generations. Activities include repairing roofs, replacing damaged materials, restoring original colors and ornaments, and engaging the local community through educational and promotional efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
